Not naturally. But that doesn’t mean they can’t be brought together. 😉

Oil and water separate because of their molecular properties. But introduce an emulsifier, and suddenly you can create something neither could become alone.

That’s the interesting part.

Sometimes the obstacle isn’t either ingredient. It’s the relationship between them.

Change the interface, change the interaction, change the outcome.

And here’s the deeper principle: Two things don’t have to become the same thing to become part of something greater.

Sometimes their differences are precisely what makes the combination valuable.

The trick is knowing when to mix, when to separate, and when to build a bridge.

